## 4. Auth flow pages — detailed spec

All three follow the same visual shell as `/login`/`/signup` (centered card, marketing layout, not the app shell). All three are local `useState` state machines — no store wiring needed, since none of this persists anything real.

### 4.1 Forgot Password (`app/forgot-password/page.tsx`)

- State: `'form' | 'sent'`.
- `form` state: a `Card` with a headline, one `Field label="Email"` + `Input type="email"`, and a `PillButton` "Send reset link". On submit (no real validation needed beyond non-empty), transition to `sent` and `toast.success('Reset link sent', 'Check your inbox for further instructions.')`.
- `sent` state: confirmation message ("If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.") plus a "Back to login" `PillLink` to `/login`, and a small "Didn't get it? Resend" text-button that just re-shows the toast and stays on this state (no actual resend logic needed).
- Small link back to `/login` in the `form` state too, for anyone who got here by mistake.

### 4.2 Reset Password (`app/reset-password/page.tsx`)

- Reads a `token` query param via `useSearchParams()` — **remember the Suspense lesson from the phase-2 patch**: wrap any component using `useSearchParams()` in a `<Suspense>` boundary, exactly the pattern used in `app/app/bots/[botId]/page.tsx` after that patch. Don't repeat that mistake here.
- If no `token` param is present at all, show an `EmptyState` (icon `AlertTriangle` or similar) — "This reset link is invalid or has expired" — with a `PillLink` back to `/forgot-password` to request a new one. This is a real, reachable state — don't skip it.
- If a token is present (any non-empty string counts as "valid" for this mock — don't build fake token validation logic), show a form: `Field label="New password"` + `Input type="password"`, `Field label="Confirm new password"` + `Input type="password"`, client-side check that they match (inline error text if not, using the same inline-validation visual pattern already used on `/signup`), `PillButton` "Reset password". On submit, transition to a `done` state — a success message plus a `PillLink` "Continue to login" → `/login`.

### 4.3 Verify Email (`app/verify-email/page.tsx`)

- Same `useSearchParams()` + `Suspense` pattern as above.
- This one has three states, driven purely by whether a token is present (no real async check — pick the state synchronously from whether the query param exists and is non-empty, so there's no artificial loading spinner needed, though a brief one is fine if you want the transition to feel real):
  - No token → `EmptyState`: "Missing verification link" with description explaining they should check their email, and a "Resend verification email" button that just fires a `toast.info('Verification email sent', "Check your inbox.")` and stays put.
  - Token present → success state: a checkmark-style confirmation ("Your email is verified"), a `PillLink` "Continue to dashboard" → `/app`.
  - (Optional, nice-to-have, not required) — if you want a third state for realism, treat a token literally equal to the string `expired` as an expired-link case with a resend button, so the page has an obviously-testable failure path. Skip this if it adds meaningful complexity; the two states above are sufficient.

